{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"00b319d7ae838cc3d3bba24368ea64c217cac19ea4aca8fe59d45eca2dc63c2f","digest":{"component_or_area":"ticket close transition and compaction","key_entities":["src/rebar/_commands/transition_close.py","src/rebar/_commands/compact_txn.py","_compact_on_close","compact_txn._compact_locked",".ticket-write.lock.d","tests/interfaces/lifecycle/test_compact_on_close_skip_7084.py","tests/interfaces/lifecycle/test_close_does_not_compact_barbet.py","tests/unit/test_transition_close.py","docs/concurrency.md","CHANGELOG.md","rebar compact","rebar._store.lock.write_lock_is_busy"],"problem_keywords":["write lock contention","compaction","store lock hold","close path performance","concurrent agent starvation"],"propositions":["Closing a ticket invokes compaction inline on the close path, holding the store write lock for minutes (measured 13m53s) while reading, reducing, and committing artifacts, starving concurrent agent writes.","The store lock hold during compaction is unbounded; nested advisory flock budgets (30s wait, 10 attempts, 3 retries, 120s timeout per git call) stack inside the held lock but never bound the total hold.","Compaction is correctness-optional housekeeping; event logs remain valid unfolded and are replayed by the reducer, so removing the inline trigger changes performance and disk size but not stored state.","Deleting _compact_on_close and its call site restores close lock-holds to seconds (matching other acquisitions: sidecar append, transition_core, signature append), leaving compaction to out-of-band triggers."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b2b5c498-2f67-4ae3-bafc-eca40294bec2","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timesta